IETA International Emissions Trading Association – formed in June 1999, it is a non-profit organisation formed by a group of companies to promote a functioning international framework for trading greenhouse gas emissions reductions. IETA members seek to develop an emissions trading regime that results in real and verifiable greenhouse gas emissions reductions, balancing economic efficiency with environmental integrity and social equity. By April 2004, IETA had grown to have 88 international companies as its member and it actively cooperates with other international organisations including the World Bank,


